e health stayed intact.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eb526cb9a4a64941","cmd-fdebaaad56ef493a","cmd-0a09106fe891405a","cmd-726ef9708bae41e2","cmd-33c5f3e0dae040f7","cmd-9a93111e725f449b","cmd-e5ad635e173b4415","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Synchronization was directly demonstrated before and after bounded node disruptions, with 5–6 second propagation and matching final data. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, recovered services and data, and successful post-restart synchronization.","limitations":["The authoritative file was absent on both nodes initially, so the executor had to initialize it; consequently, the evidence cannot demonstrate preservation of any pre-existing application configuration.","Only two changes were timed, although both were far below 15 minutes and the enabled five-minute fallback timer supports continued compliance."]}
